[0.03,"ro",{"on":"Reply with the single word FIVE. Do not use any tools.","enter":false,"while_screen_contains":"Ask Codex to do anything","data":"\u001b[2J\u001b[H› Write a 400 word story about a lighthouse keeper. Do not use any tools.                                                  “I found this in a wreck,” he said. “The name on it is Vale.”                                                                                                                                                                                     Mara opened the box. Inside lay her father’s brass compass, its glass cracked, its needle still trembling toward north.  Beneath it rested a scrap of paper in his familiar hand: “Tell Mara the light reached us. We saw it before the boat      went under.”                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      For a long moment, she could not speak. Then she set the compass beside the lamp and climbed the stairs. The stranger    followed, silent as she opened the shutters.                                                                                                                                                                                                      The beam turned over the sea. Once, twice, again. Far out, a ship answered with three short flashes. Mara watched until  the vessel cleared the rocks and vanished into calmer darkness.                                                                                                                                                                                   Afterward, she poured tea for herself and the stranger. She asked his name, and he told her. She asked where he had      found the box, and he described a beach beyond the headland, where the tide had carried wreckage ashore.                                                                                                                                          Before dawn, he left for the village. Mara stayed beside the lamp. Her father had seen the light; somehow, that was      enough. At sunset she would climb the stairs again, carrying her cup, tending the flame, and keeping her promise for     everyone still at sea.                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Worked for 10s • 9:52 AM                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 › Reply with the single word FOUR. Do not use any tools.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   • FOUR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Worked for 1s • 9:53 AM                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  › Reply with the single word FIVE. Do not use any tools.                             